# Raw per-flow iperf3 output — bulky (E2 2h run ≈ 67 MB), regenerable.
# Analysis (analyze_e1.py / analyze_e2.py) reads these; the derived summaries
# and the per-second CPU logs are what we keep.
*_flow*.json
*.err

# Run transcripts (stdout of a driver) — not measurements.
rep*.log
*_run.log
e2_2h.log
alignment_run.log
blindness_run.log

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The repo-root .gitignore has a blanket `*.log` (Node template) that also
# swallows E1/E2's CPU-over-time logs — those ARE the measurement, keep them.
!*_hostcpu.log
!*_containercpu.log
